\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces The perturbation--pruning paradox. (a)\nobreakspace  {}Per-message perturbation impact: acknowledgments (ACKs) are the most locally disruptive message type (median similarity $= 0.34$ after removal vs.\ $0.50$ for non-ACK types; $n = 450$ each, Qwen2.5-7B, GSM8K). Lower similarity indicates greater disruption to subsequent dialogue. (b)\nobreakspace  {}Yet bulk removal of \emph  {all} acknowledgments preserves task accuracy across configurations. $\bullet $ = single seed; $\blacklozenge $ = multi-seed mean $\pm $ 95\% CI. Green band: $\pm 1$\,pp TOST equivalence; blue band: $-3$\,pp non-inferiority margin. The Llama/StratQA single-seed point ($+5.0$\,pp) reflects high variance under longer reasoning chains ($N{=}238$).\relax }}{2}{figure.caption.2}\protected@file@percent }
\providecommand*\caption@xref[2]{\@setref\relax\@undefined{#1}}
\newlabel{fig:paradox}{{1}{2}{The perturbation--pruning paradox. (a)~Per-message perturbation impact: acknowledgments (ACKs) are the most locally disruptive message type (median similarity $= 0.34$ after removal vs.\ $0.50$ for non-ACK types; $n = 450$ each, Qwen2.5-7B, GSM8K). Lower similarity indicates greater disruption to subsequent dialogue. (b)~Yet bulk removal of \emph {all} acknowledgments preserves task accuracy across configurations. $\bullet $ = single seed; $\blacklozenge $ = multi-seed mean $\pm $ 95\% CI. Green band: $\pm 1$\,pp TOST equivalence; blue band: $-3$\,pp non-inferiority margin. The Llama/StratQA single-seed point ($+5.0$\,pp) reflects high variance under longer reasoning chains ($N{=}238$).\relax }{figure.caption.2}{}}
