\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces (a)\nobreakspace  {}Remove-ablation similarity by function type (Qwen2.5-7B, $n{=}895$). Lower $=$ greater disruption; acknowledgments (acks; median $= 0.34$) most impactful despite least information. The COORD boxplot ($n{=}5$) should be interpreted with caution given the small sample size. (b)\nobreakspace  {}Cumulative type-elimination dose-response (None $\to $ ACK $\to $ +COORD $\to $ +INFO $\to $ All-RG). Qwen holds within 1\,pp through +INFO; only All-RG (70\% suppression) reaches significance. Llama drops sharply at +INFO (68\% suppression). Error bars: 95\% CIs from McNemar's discordant pairs.\relax }}{7}{figure.caption.15}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:impact_and_dose}{{2}{7}{(a)~Remove-ablation similarity by function type (Qwen2.5-7B, $n{=}895$). Lower $=$ greater disruption; acknowledgments (acks; median $= 0.34$) most impactful despite least information. The COORD boxplot ($n{=}5$) should be interpreted with caution given the small sample size. (b)~Cumulative type-elimination dose-response (None $\to $ ACK $\to $ +COORD $\to $ +INFO $\to $ All-RG). Qwen holds within 1\,pp through +INFO; only All-RG (70\% suppression) reaches significance. Llama drops sharply at +INFO (68\% suppression). Error bars: 95\% CIs from McNemar's discordant pairs.\relax }{figure.caption.15}{}}
\newlabel{fig:impact}{{2}{7}{(a)~Remove-ablation similarity by function type (Qwen2.5-7B, $n{=}895$). Lower $=$ greater disruption; acknowledgments (acks; median $= 0.34$) most impactful despite least information. The COORD boxplot ($n{=}5$) should be interpreted with caution given the small sample size. (b)~Cumulative type-elimination dose-response (None $\to $ ACK $\to $ +COORD $\to $ +INFO $\to $ All-RG). Qwen holds within 1\,pp through +INFO; only All-RG (70\% suppression) reaches significance. Llama drops sharply at +INFO (68\% suppression). Error bars: 95\% CIs from McNemar's discordant pairs.\relax }{figure.caption.15}{}}
\newlabel{fig:dose_response}{{2}{7}{(a)~Remove-ablation similarity by function type (Qwen2.5-7B, $n{=}895$). Lower $=$ greater disruption; acknowledgments (acks; median $= 0.34$) most impactful despite least information. The COORD boxplot ($n{=}5$) should be interpreted with caution given the small sample size. (b)~Cumulative type-elimination dose-response (None $\to $ ACK $\to $ +COORD $\to $ +INFO $\to $ All-RG). Qwen holds within 1\,pp through +INFO; only All-RG (70\% suppression) reaches significance. Llama drops sharply at +INFO (68\% suppression). Error bars: 95\% CIs from McNemar's discordant pairs.\relax }{figure.caption.15}{}}
